FIX 6 — Create supabase/migrations/fix_consultation_rls.sql. The file must DROP the two broken policies and CREATE corrected ones that reference admin_profiles instead of profiles, and remove the .role check (admin_profiles only has 'high'/'low' roles, not 'admin'/'super_admin'). SQL content:
  DROP POLICY IF EXISTS "Admins can view all consultation requests" ON consultation_requests;
  DROP POLICY IF EXISTS "Admins can update consultation requests" ON consultation_requests;
  CREATE POLICY "Admins can view all consultation requests"
    ON consultation_requests FOR SELECT TO authenticated
    USING (EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM admin_profiles WHERE admin_profiles.id = auth.uid()));
  CREATE POLICY "Admins can update consultation requests"
    ON consultation_requests FOR UPDATE TO authenticated
    USING (EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM admin_profiles WHERE admin_profiles.id = auth.uid()))
    WITH CHECK (EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM admin_profiles WHERE admin_profiles.id = auth.uid()));
Also create supabase/migrations/fix_consultation_rls.md with instructions to run this SQL in the Supabase SQL Editor.
